1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,467
Green velvet moss on a wall.

2
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:04,735
Thin brown stalks rising from it.

3
00:00:04,735 --> 00:00:06,802
Brown dots under a fern leaf.

4
00:00:07,202 --> 00:00:09,064
They look like small details.

5
00:00:09,064 --> 00:00:12,611
But each one belongs to a
different generation of a plant.

6
00:00:13,061 --> 00:00:15,884
Diya noticed the brown
stalks after the monsoon.

7
00:00:15,884 --> 00:00:19,879
She asked: is that stalk part of
the moss, or a different plant?

8
00:00:20,229 --> 00:00:21,206
It is both.

9
00:00:21,206 --> 00:00:24,387
The moss lives two lives,
and they take turns.

10
00:00:24,887 --> 00:00:28,761
By the end, you will know the two
generations, the two switches between

11
00:00:28,761 --> 00:00:30,724
them, and how to spot each one.

12
00:00:31,374 --> 00:00:32,961
So what are the two lives?

13
00:00:33,311 --> 00:00:35,234
The first is the gametophyte.

14
00:00:35,234 --> 00:00:37,792
Gameto means gamete, phyte means plant.

15
00:00:37,792 --> 00:00:41,109
It is the plant that makes
gametes, the sex cells.

16
00:00:41,559 --> 00:00:45,143
The second is the sporophyte,
the plant that makes spores.

17
00:00:45,143 --> 00:00:49,387
A spore is a single cell that can
grow into a new plant on its own.

18
00:00:49,837 --> 00:00:52,126
Each one gives rise to the other.

19
00:00:52,126 --> 00:00:55,541
Gametophyte, then sporophyte,
then gametophyte again.

20
00:00:55,541 --> 00:00:57,810
That is alternation of generations.

21
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:00,674
Let's zoom into the moss on the wall.

22
00:01:01,024 --> 00:01:03,839
The green, leafy plant is the gametophyte.

23
00:01:03,839 --> 00:01:06,909
Rhizoids, thin threads,
hold it to the wall.

24
00:01:07,409 --> 00:01:09,880
The brown stalk on top is the sporophyte.

25
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:13,318
It has a foot, a stalk called
the seta, and a capsule.

26
00:01:13,818 --> 00:01:15,592
Zoom into the capsule.

27
00:01:15,592 --> 00:01:19,197
Inside, cells divide by
meiosis and make spores.

28
00:01:19,697 --> 00:01:21,118
Zoom into one spore.

29
00:01:21,118 --> 00:01:25,135
It carries one set of chromosomes,
the instructions of the cell.

30
00:01:25,135 --> 00:01:27,454
It can grow into a new green moss.

31
00:01:28,104 --> 00:01:30,018
Now let's run the whole cycle.

32
00:01:30,368 --> 00:01:31,268
Step one.

33
00:01:31,165 --> 00:01:34,702
The gametophyte makes gametes:
male gametes and an egg.

34
00:01:35,452 --> 00:01:36,352
Step two.

35
00:01:36,281 --> 00:01:39,352
A male gamete swims
through water to the egg.

36
00:01:39,352 --> 00:01:40,252
They fuse.

37
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:43,342
This is fertilisation,
and it makes a zygote.

38
00:01:44,092 --> 00:01:45,002
Step three.

39
00:01:45,002 --> 00:01:49,266
The zygote divides again and again,
and grows into the sporophyte.

40
00:01:50,016 --> 00:01:50,963
Step four.

41
00:01:50,963 --> 00:01:55,042
In the capsule, cells divide
by meiosis and make spores.

42
00:01:55,792 --> 00:01:56,706
Step five.

43
00:01:56,706 --> 00:02:00,928
A spore lands on wet ground and
grows into a new gametophyte.

44
00:02:00,928 --> 00:02:02,598
The cycle turns again.

45
00:02:03,348 --> 00:02:05,442
So two events act like switches.

46
00:02:05,792 --> 00:02:09,808
Fertilisation switches the cycle from
the gametophyte to the sporophyte.

47
00:02:10,558 --> 00:02:14,410
Meiosis switches it back, from
the sporophyte to the gametophyte.

48
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:19,991
Between the switches, cells grow by
mitosis, a division that makes exact

49
00:02:19,991 --> 00:02:20,891
copies.

50
00:02:21,439 --> 00:02:24,294
Let's put the two
generations side by side.

51
00:02:24,644 --> 00:02:27,856
The gametophyte starts from
a spore and makes gametes.

52
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:30,470
In a moss, it is the green leafy plant.

53
00:02:30,470 --> 00:02:33,737
In a fern, it is a small,
heart shaped prothallus.

54
00:02:34,187 --> 00:02:37,354
The sporophyte starts from
a zygote and makes spores.

55
00:02:37,354 --> 00:02:40,585
In a moss, it is the brown
stalk with its capsule.

56
00:02:40,585 --> 00:02:43,439
In a fern, it is the
big leafy fern itself.

57
00:02:44,089 --> 00:02:44,989
Your turn.

58
00:02:44,989 --> 00:02:50,115
The fern in the corridor pot has brown
dots full of spores under its leaves.

59
00:02:50,115 --> 00:02:52,610
Which generation is that fern plant?

60
00:02:52,610 --> 00:02:53,936
Pause and decide.

61
00:02:57,136 --> 00:02:58,140
The sporophyte!

62
00:02:58,140 --> 00:03:00,821
It makes spores, so it is the spore plant.

63
00:03:01,471 --> 00:03:02,558
Remember this.

64
00:03:02,558 --> 00:03:04,886
Fertilisation starts the sporophyte.

65
00:03:04,886 --> 00:03:08,270
Meiosis makes the spores
that start the gametophyte.

66
00:03:08,870 --> 00:03:10,435
Now, a worked example.

67
00:03:10,435 --> 00:03:12,777
Let's walk around the life of a fern.

68
00:03:13,127 --> 00:03:15,290
The big fern is the sporophyte.

69
00:03:15,290 --> 00:03:18,674
Under its leaves, sporangia
make spores by meiosis.

70
00:03:19,124 --> 00:03:23,821
A spore lands on cool, damp soil,
and grows into a small prothallus.

71
00:03:23,821 --> 00:03:25,535
That is the gametophyte.

72
00:03:25,985 --> 00:03:28,699
The prothallus makes
male gametes and eggs.

73
00:03:28,699 --> 00:03:31,779
The male gametes need
water to swim to the egg.

74
00:03:32,229 --> 00:03:37,086
Fertilisation makes a zygote, and
the zygote grows into a new big fern.

75
00:03:37,086 --> 00:03:39,255
Two generations, taking turns.

76
00:03:39,905 --> 00:03:41,370
Now, the exam trap.

77
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:45,913
Many students think the gametophyte
makes its gametes by meiosis, like

78
00:03:45,913 --> 00:03:46,813
we do.

79
00:03:46,965 --> 00:03:50,642
But the gametophyte already
has one set of chromosomes.

80
00:03:50,642 --> 00:03:52,668
It makes gametes by mitosis.

81
00:03:52,668 --> 00:03:56,283
In these plants, meiosis
makes spores, not gametes.

82
00:03:56,933 --> 00:03:58,355
Where is this asked?

83
00:03:58,355 --> 00:04:02,716
As statements about which generation
makes spores or gametes, and by which

84
00:04:02,716 --> 00:04:03,616
division.

85
00:04:04,041 --> 00:04:05,259
Exam level now.

86
00:04:05,259 --> 00:04:07,055
Read the four statements.

87
00:04:07,055 --> 00:04:08,748
Which ones are correct?

88
00:04:08,748 --> 00:04:10,017
Pause and solve.

89
00:04:15,417 --> 00:04:16,643
The answer is C.

90
00:04:16,643 --> 00:04:18,732
Statements one, three and four.

91
00:04:19,232 --> 00:04:20,371
Two is wrong.

92
00:04:20,371 --> 00:04:23,452
The gametophyte makes
its gametes by mitosis.

93
00:04:23,952 --> 00:04:26,723
The sporophyte makes spores by meiosis.

94
00:04:26,723 --> 00:04:28,953
The zygote is its first cell.

95
00:04:28,953 --> 00:04:32,114
And spores grow into
gametophytes by mitosis.

96
00:04:32,714 --> 00:04:34,173
Here is your recap.

97
00:04:34,173 --> 00:04:35,673
Screenshot this card.

98
00:04:38,873 --> 00:04:41,709
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

99
00:04:42,109 --> 00:04:43,009
One.

100
00:04:42,678 --> 00:04:44,898
Which generation makes spores?

101
00:04:45,798 --> 00:04:46,698
Two.

102
00:04:46,293 --> 00:04:49,677
Which two events switch one
generation into the other?

103
00:04:50,577 --> 00:04:51,477
Three.

104
00:04:51,207 --> 00:04:54,443
In a fern, which generation
is the prothallus?

105
00:04:55,543 --> 00:05:00,575
Next time: why does one plant body carry
twice the chromosomes of the other?

106
00:05:00,575 --> 00:05:03,429
We find out in haploid and diploid phases.
